 "about_text": "Sean Kelly is a contemporary art gallery founded in 1991 by dealer Sean Kelly, originally opening its first public space on Mercer Street in SoHo before moving to a larger Chelsea location in 2001 and then to its current 22,000-square-foot building at 475 Tenth Avenue in 2012. In 2021 the gallery expanded to Los Angeles, opening a second space at 1357 N Highland Avenue. Known for an intellectually driven, internationally oriented program, Sean Kelly represents a diverse roster spanning painting, sculpture, photography, and performance, including figures such as Marina Abramović, Kehinde Wiley, and Idris Khan, alongside a growing group of emerging artists. The gallery is active on the international art-fair circuit and regularly collaborates with major museums worldwide.",
